{"openapi":"3.1.0","info":{"title":"Invokely statistics API","version":"1.0.0","description":"Official statistics with unit, period, normalized place and citable source. Same operations as the MCP server at /mcp."},"servers":[{"url":"https://invokely.ai"}],"components":{"securitySchemes":{"bearer":{"type":"http","scheme":"bearer","description":"API key (ivk_...) or OAuth access token."},"apiKey":{"type":"apiKey","in":"header","name":"x-api-key"}}},"security":[{"bearer":[]},{"apiKey":[]},{}],"paths":{"/api/v1/indicators":{"get":{"operationId":"searchIndicators","summary":"Search indicators","description":"Find official statistical indicators by natural language, in English or Spanish. Use this first when you do not know the exact indicator id.\nCoverage: Spain (municipalities, provinces, regions, national), EU countries, the United States (nation, states, counties), and every country plus the World from the World Bank. Topics: population and demography, unemployment and employment, prices and inflation, income, GDP, housing, companies, tourism, interest rates, public finance.\nPass geography when the question is about a specific place: only indicators with data for that place are listed, and matches published elsewhere are named in not_available_for_place.\nExample: {\"query\": \"tasa de paro\", \"geography\": \"Mataró\"}.\nReturns {indicators: [{id, name, unit, frequencies, levels, definition, note?}], place?, not_available_for_place?}. Read note: it explains common confusions, such as survey unemployment rate versus registered unemployment.","parameters":[{"name":"q","in":"query","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"geography","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"locale","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["en","es"]}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Success. Body is {\"data\": ...}."},"400":{"description":"Invalid argument."},"401":{"description":"Invalid API key."},"402":{"description":"Allowance used up."},"404":{"description":"Unknown indicator or place, or no data."},"429":{"description":"Rate limited."}}}},"/api/v1/places/resolve":{"get":{"operationId":"resolvePlace","summary":"Resolve a place","description":"Turn a place name into the normalized entity Invokely uses, with its official codes (INE, Idescat, NUTS, ISO, US FIPS) and parent.\nUse it when a name is ambiguous or you want to confirm which entity a number refers to. The other tools accept names directly, so this call is optional.\nAmbiguous names prefer the municipality (\"Barcelona\" is the city); the province and region come back in alternatives. Ask for \"provincia de Barcelona\" to get the province.\nUS states are regions and US counties are provinces. Names shared by several places of the same level, such as \"Washington County\", return an AMBIGUOUS_PLACE error with suggestions; add the state (\"Washington County, Oregon\") or pass a suggested id.\nExample: {\"name\": \"Mataró\"}. Returns {match: {id, name, level, country, population, parent, codes}, alternatives: [{id, name, level}]}.","parameters":[{"name":"name","in":"query","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"country","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 code."},{"name":"level","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["municipality","province","region","country","supranational"]}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Success. Body is {\"data\": ...}."},"400":{"description":"Invalid argument."},"401":{"description":"Invalid API key."},"402":{"description":"Allowance used up."},"404":{"description":"Unknown indicator or place, or no data."},"429":{"description":"Rate limited."}}}},"/api/v1/value":{"get":{"operationId":"getValue","summary":"Get one value","description":"Get one official figure for an indicator and place: the latest by default, or a given period.\nUse it for questions like \"population of Mataró\", \"inflation in Spain in 2024-09\", \"unemployment rate in Cataluña\", \"unemployment rate in Texas\".\nExample: {\"indicator\": \"population\", \"place\": \"Mataró\"}.\nReturns {indicator: {id, name, unit}, place: {id, name, level}, period, value, status?, source: {name, title, url, retrieved, published?, citation, inputs?}, note?}. note is a caveat about the source series served.\nAlways cite source.citation or source.url when you answer. status \"provisional\" or \"estimated\" means the figure may be revised; say so. status \"low_reliability\" means the publisher flags the figure as of low reliability (usually a small survey sample); say so and treat it as a rough indication.\nIf the indicator is not published for that place you get an error that names the levels where it exists and related indicators that do have data.","parameters":[{"name":"indicator","in":"query","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"Indicator id, for example population or registered_unemployment_rate."},{"name":"place","in":"query","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"Place name or id, for example Mataró, es-mun-08121, ES51."},{"name":"period","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"2024, 2024-Q3, 2024-S1 or 2024-09."},{"name":"frequency","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["year","half","quarter","month"]}},{"name":"country","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 code."},{"name":"locale","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["en","es"]}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Success. Body is {\"data\": ...}."},"400":{"description":"Invalid argument."},"401":{"description":"Invalid API key."},"402":{"description":"Allowance used up."},"404":{"description":"Unknown indicator or place, or no data."},"429":{"description":"Rate limited."}}}},"/api/v1/series":{"get":{"operationId":"getSeries","summary":"Get a time series","description":"Get the time series of an indicator for one place, oldest to newest, from one source so the points are comparable.\nUse it for trends: \"evolution of the CPI by month\", \"population of Mataró since 2015\".\nExample: {\"indicator\": \"cpi_annual_change\", \"place\": \"España\", \"from\": \"2023-01\"}.\nReturns {indicator, place, frequency, points: [[period, value], ...], total_points, truncated?, flags?: {period: status}, gaps?, source, other_frequencies?, longer_history?, note?, projections_available?}. gaps lists periods the source did not publish.\nProjections (for example population to 2050) are never mixed into points. Pass include_projections: true to get them in a separate projections block {label, vintage, points, source}; always say a projected figure is a projection.\nFree and Builder plans receive 60 points: the latest ones, or the first ones from \"from\" when you pass it. truncated says when history was cut.","parameters":[{"name":"indicator","in":"query","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"Indicator id, for example population or registered_unemployment_rate."},{"name":"place","in":"query","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"Place name or id, for example Mataró, es-mun-08121, ES51."},{"name":"from","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"to","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"frequency","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["year","half","quarter","month"]}},{"name":"country","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 code."},{"name":"locale","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["en","es"]}},{"name":"include_projections","in":"query","schema":{"type":"boolean"},"description":"Also return the publisher projections after the last observed period, in a separate projections block."}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Success. Body is {\"data\": ...}."},"400":{"description":"Invalid argument."},"401":{"description":"Invalid API key."},"402":{"description":"Allowance used up."},"404":{"description":"Unknown indicator or place, or no data."},"429":{"description":"Rate limited."}}}},"/api/v1/compare":{"get":{"operationId":"compare","summary":"Compare places","description":"Compare one indicator across 2 to 10 places for the same period, using one shared source and definition whenever possible.\nUse it for \"how does X compare with Y and Z\". Places can mix levels, for example a city, a larger city and its region.\nExample: {\"indicator\": \"registered_unemployment_rate\", \"places\": [\"Mataró\", \"Barcelona\", \"Cataluña\"]}.\nReturns {indicator, period, comparable, values: [{place, value, period?, status?}], source or sources, notes?}. When comparable is false the values come from different sources (and sometimes periods) and notes explain why; mention it in your answer.\nFor unemployment in municipalities use registered_unemployment_rate: the survey unemployment_rate is not published below province level.","parameters":[{"name":"indicator","in":"query","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"Indicator id, for example population or registered_unemployment_rate."},{"name":"place","in":"query","required":true,"schema":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"style":"form","explode":true,"description":"Repeat for each place (2 to 10)."},{"name":"period","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"2024, 2024-Q3, 2024-S1 or 2024-09."},{"name":"country","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 code."},{"name":"locale","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["en","es"]}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Success. Body is {\"data\": ...}."},"400":{"description":"Invalid argument."},"401":{"description":"Invalid API key."},"402":{"description":"Allowance used up."},"404":{"description":"Unknown indicator or place, or no data."},"429":{"description":"Rate limited."}}}},"/api/v1/rank":{"get":{"operationId":"rankPlaces","summary":"Rank places","description":"Rank every place of one level inside an area by an indicator: all countries of the world, EU countries, US states, the counties of a state, the regions of a country, the municipalities of a Spanish province.\nUse it for \"which state has the highest unemployment\", \"top 10 countries by GDP per capita\", \"poorest counties in Texas\", \"EU countries with the lowest inflation\".\nlevel is the level of the ranked places (country, region, province, municipality); within is the area they belong to. US states are regions of \"United States\"; US counties are provinces of a state; EU NUTS 2 regions are regions of \"EU\" or of a country.\nExample: {\"indicator\": \"unemployment_rate\", \"level\": \"region\", \"within\": \"United States\", \"limit\": 5}. Countries of the world: {\"indicator\": \"population\", \"level\": \"country\"}.\nReturns {indicator, level, within, period, comparable, order, total, values: [{rank, place, value, status?}], source, notes?}. Every value comes from one source and one period. order \"asc\" lists the lowest first. Cite source.citation.\nFor rates across municipalities pass min_population (for example 5000) so very small places, where a few people move the rate, do not top the list.","parameters":[{"name":"indicator","in":"query","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"Indicator id, for example population or registered_unemployment_rate."},{"name":"level","in":"query","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","enum":["country","region","province","municipality"]}},{"name":"within","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"Area whose places are ranked, for example \"United States\", \"Germany\", \"Texas\". Omit to rank every country."},{"name":"period","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"2024, 2024-Q3, 2024-S1 or 2024-09."},{"name":"order","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["desc","asc"]}},{"name":"limit","in":"query","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":100}},{"name":"min_population","in":"query","schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"description":"Leave out places with fewer residents, for example 5000."},{"name":"country","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 code."},{"name":"locale","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["en","es"]}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Success. Body is {\"data\": ...}."},"400":{"description":"Invalid argument."},"401":{"description":"Invalid API key."},"402":{"description":"Allowance used up."},"404":{"description":"Unknown indicator or place, or no data."},"429":{"description":"Rate limited."}}}},"/api/v1/export.csv":{"get":{"operationId":"exportCsv","summary":"Export a series as CSV (Pro plan or prepaid credits)","parameters":[{"name":"indicator","in":"query","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"Indicator id, for example population or registered_unemployment_rate."},{"name":"place","in":"query","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string"},"description":"Place name or id, for example Mataró, es-mun-08121, ES51."},{"name":"from","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"to","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string"}},{"name":"frequency","in":"query","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["year","half","quarter","month"]}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"CSV file."},"402":{"description":"Plan required."}}}},"/api/v1/catalog":{"get":{"operationId":"catalog","summary":"List every indicator (free)","security":[],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Catalog."}}}},"/api/v1/indicators/{id}":{"get":{"operationId":"getIndicator","summary":"Indicator definition (free)","security":[],"parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Definition."},"404":{"description":"Unknown indicator."}}}},"/api/v1/sources":{"get":{"operationId":"sources","summary":"Sources, licenses and status (free)","security":[],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Sources."}}}},"/api/v1/usage":{"get":{"operationId":"usage","summary":"Usage for the authenticated account (free)","responses":{"200":{"description":"Usage summary."},"401":{"description":"API key required."}}}}}}